@startuml openai_block
title K9-AIF with the OpenAI Agents SDK: block view

rectangle "K9-AIF application" {
  rectangle "Router / Orchestrator / Squad" as Caller
  rectangle "Shield governance\n(ingress, egress, tool result)" as Shield
  rectangle "Tool gate\n(registry, record checks, rules)" as Gate
  rectangle "HIL Orchestrator\n-> k9x HIL" as HIL
  rectangle "Model Router\n(eligibility, learned scores)" as Router
}

rectangle "Adapter (sole broker)" {
  rectangle "OpenAIAgentsOrchestratorAdapter" as Adapter
  rectangle "K9ToolGuardrail\n(every function tool)" as TG
  rectangle "K9ModelProvider\n+ K9GovernedModel" as MP
}

rectangle "OpenAI Agents SDK" {
  rectangle "Runner\n(agent loop, handoffs)" as Runner
}

rectangle "OpenAI-compatible model\n(OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Ollama, vLLM)" as Model
rectangle "Tool handlers\n(registered capabilities)" as Tools

Caller --> Adapter : 1. request
Adapter --> Shield : 2. ingress check
Adapter --> Runner : 3. run (agent built by adapter)
Runner --> MP : 4. every model call
MP --> Router : route()
MP --> Model : call chosen model
Runner --> TG : 5. every tool call
TG --> Shield : tool args / result
TG --> Gate : propose()
Gate --> HIL : irreversible or mismatch
TG --> Tools : allowed call
Adapter --> Shield : 6. final output check
Adapter --> Caller : 7. governed result

note bottom of Runner
  Hosted tools (web search, file search,
  code interpreter, hosted MCP) run on
  OpenAI servers. The adapter refuses
  them unless explicitly allowed.
end note
@enduml
